2. FFmpeg — libavcodec / libavutil (LGPL-2.1-or-later)

AAC-LC decoding links FFmpeg's libavcodec and libavutil through cgo
(`internal/aac/aac.go`: `#cgo pkg-config: libavcodec libavutil`), the same
decoder the upstream receiver uses for AAC buffered streams. FFmpeg is licensed
under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later (upstream
https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg). Only a single decoder is used.

The device packages are built from the FFmpeg 7.1 release tarball, which is the
source of record (no git checkout is involved; the tarball's own `VERSION` and
`RELEASE` files read `7.1`):

    url:    https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-7.1.tar.xz
    sha256: 40973d44970dbc83ef302b0609f2e74982be2d85916dd2ee7472d30678a7abe6

`apps/airplay/target/pins.sh` pins that URL and digest; the tarball is verified
against the digest before it is built, and `apps/airplay/target/container/ffmpeg.sh`
is the single source of the configure line:

    --prefix=/opt/ffmpeg --enable-static --disable-shared --disable-programs --disable-doc
    --disable-network --disable-everything --enable-decoder=aac --enable-parser=aac
    --disable-zlib --disable-bzlib --disable-lzma --disable-iconv --disable-xlib --disable-sdl2
    --disable-avdevice --disable-swscale --disable-swresample --disable-postproc --disable-avfilter
    --disable-avformat --disable-autodetect --enable-pic --cc=gcc

No GPL-only FFmpeg component is enabled, and the build produces only
`libavcodec.a` and `libavutil.a` (the recipe fails if a shared libavcodec or
libavutil appears in the prefix).

LGPL obligations for this link — **the branch is static**:

- The device packages (`apps/airplay/target/`) link `libavcodec.a` and
  `libavutil.a` statically. `readelf -d` on the packaged binary shows no
  `libavcodec`/`libavutil` entry, and the FFmpeg prefix contains no shared
  object. The dynamic branch of LGPL §6 (ship the `.so` files and a loader
  path) therefore does not apply to them.
- Because the link is static, LGPL-2.1+ section 6 is a **distribution
  precondition**: alongside every package the build publishes the relinkable
  object archive, the exact archives that were linked, the corresponding FFmpeg
  source (URL and sha256 above), the configure line, and the relink procedure
  (`RELINK.md`). The layout is listed under "Relinking the statically linked
  decoder" below. Shipping the package without that directory is not compliant.
- A host (development) build in `apps/airplay/build.sh` still links FFmpeg
  dynamically where the host's FFmpeg provides shared libraries; nothing in the
  repository forces static linking or hidden symbol resolution.
- The FFmpeg library is not modified by this project; if it ever were, the
  modifications would have to be provided under the LGPL as well.

