## Relinking the statically linked decoder (LGPL-2.1+ obligation)

The device packages link FFmpeg's `libavcodec.a` and `libavutil.a` statically
(the AAC decoder only; the build is `apps/airplay/target/build-target.sh`). Under
LGPL-2.1+ section 6, distribution of a work that statically links those
libraries requires that the recipient be able to relink the work against a
modified version of the libraries. Each target package's build therefore also
publishes, beside the package, this exact layout:

```
<OUT>/lgpl/<abi>/
  objects.tar.gz        every object file and package archive the link consumed,
                        in the bNNN/ layout the Go toolchain used, with
                        build-commands.log (the verbatim `go build -work -x`
                        transcript, including the final `gcc` link line) and
                        b001/importcfg.link
  libavcodec.a          the exact archives that were linked
  libavutil.a
  ffmpeg-7.1.tar.xz     the corresponding FFmpeg source (sha256 above)
  SOURCE.txt            version, url, sha256, tarball RELEASE/VERSION
  configure-line.txt    the exact configure line quoted in §2
  RELINK.md             both relink procedures: relink the objects, or rebuild
                        from source against a modified FFmpeg
  NOTICE                this file
```

The archive is built with the same flags as the packaged binary, so replacing
`libavcodec.a`/`libavutil.a` with a modified build and re-running the recorded
link command (or rebuilding the app from source against the modified prefix)
produces a working replacement binary. There is no written-offer fallback: the
material itself ships with the package.

The offer is valid for three years from distribution, and nothing here claims
FFmpeg is licensed under this repository's terms: FFmpeg remains
LGPL-2.1-or-later, Copyright its authors.
